SDL2 window port -- build notes
================================

This is a scaffold: it gives UnNetHack a real graphical window and a real
event loop, with map/message/status/menu content drawn as colored glyphs
via SDL2_ttf. It does not yet draw the pixel tile art from win/share --
see "Known gaps" below.

Dependencies
------------
  - SDL2
  - SDL2_ttf
  - a monospace TrueType font on the build machine (the port tries a
    short list of common macOS/Linux paths at startup; see
    sdl_font_candidates in win/sdl/sdlmain.c if yours isn't found)

macOS (Homebrew):
    brew install sdl2 sdl2_ttf

Debian/Ubuntu:
    apt install libsdl2-dev libsdl2-ttf-dev

Enabling the port
------------------
1. In include/config.h, uncomment:
       #define SDL_GRAPHICS

   Leave whatever other *_GRAPHICS port you already use defined too if
   you want both available at runtime (selectable via -windowtype sdl
   or the WINDOWTYPE resource/config option); just make sure exactly
   one is picked as DEFAULT_WINDOW_SYS, which SDL_GRAPHICS will do
   automatically if it's the only one defined.

2. In sys/unix/Makefile.src:
     - Set the windowing-system selector to the SDL block:
           WINSRC = $(WINSDLSRC)
           WINOBJ = $(WINSDLOBJ)
     - Set:
           WINLIB = $(WINSDLLIB)
     - Uncomment (and adjust for your platform) one of the SDL2
       CFLAGS/LFLAGS example pairs near the top of the file, so the
       compiler and linker can find <SDL2/SDL.h> and libSDL2.

3. Build as usual from sys/unix (configure/Makefile.top per the
   existing UnNetHack unix build instructions).

Known gaps (intentionally deferred, not bugs)
-----------------------------------------------
  - No pixel tile art -- map cells render as a single colored character
    per glyph (via the same mapglyph() lookup tty/curses use), not the
    bitmap tiles in win/share. Wiring those in is the natural next
    step; win/X11/tile2x11.c is the reference for how an existing port
    turns win/share's tile data into blittable pixels.
  - No real role/race/gender/alignment selection dialog
    (sdl_player_selection() is a no-op; unset facets fall back to the
    game's normal "pick at random" behavior). See
    win/tty/wintty.c:tty_player_selection for what a full dialog looks
    like.
  - No persistent inventory window (WC_PERM_INVENT not advertised).
  - No message history scrollback viewer (sdl_doprev_message() is a
    stub) -- full history is kept internally, just not wired to a key.
  - Font/DPI handling is minimal: one fixed point size, no HiDPI
    scaling.
  - SDL_QUIT (closing the window) ends the process immediately via
    nh_terminate() rather than going through a save-game confirmation.
